# Changelog

All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.

The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/),
and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html).

## [1.0.8] - 2026-07-23

Security and dependency hygiene. These changes are in devDependencies and the
docs site; the published package (`dist/`, no runtime dependencies) is unchanged.

### Security

- Fix all pnpm audit advisories (15 to 0): bump `next` to 16.2.11 and `hono`
  to 4.12.27, override `sharp` to 0.35.0 and `brace-expansion` to 2.1.2
- Move the website to `@hono/node-server` 2.x, which patches the `serve-static`
  path traversal. 2.x dropped the `/vercel` subpath, so the Vercel adapter now
  builds its handler from `getRequestListener` (what 1.x's `handle` did internally)

## [1.0.7] - 2026-07-22

### Fixed

- Fix the dev warning logged when the App Router context is unavailable

### Changed

- Documentation site is now agent-ready (serves Markdown via content
  negotiation, plus `robots.txt` and `sitemap.xml`)
- Remove em dashes from the docs and README

## [1.0.6] - 2026-07-07

### Changed

- Point the package homepage at the Vercel docs site
- Serve the documentation site as a Vercel function instead of static files

## [1.0.5] - 2026-06-18

### Added

- Documentation website

### Changed

- Replace the Tailwind CDN with build-time CSS, update npm metadata
- Add Next.js 16.2 to CI

### Security

- Fix all pnpm audit advisories (61 to 0)

## [1.0.3] - 2026-03-18

### Fixed

- Fix `isSetup` ref blocking link interceptor re-initialization when App Router
  context transitions from null to non-null
- Fix `refresh()` passing full URL (`location.href`) as the `to` parameter, now
  using `location.pathname + location.search` for consistency with push/replace
- Fix `"types"` condition order in package.json exports (must be first per TypeScript docs)
- Remove incorrect `"module"` field pointing to CJS output

### Changed

- CI now uses `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` for reproducible builds

## [1.0.2] - 2026-03-18

### Fixed

- Fix accepted link clicks causing a full page reload instead of client-side navigation,
  now using the App Router ref instead of `window.next?.router` (Pages Router artifact)
- Add `appRouter` to effect dependency array so link interceptor re-initializes
  if router context changes after hydration
- Skip non-HTTP protocol links (`mailto:`, `tel:`, `blob:`, etc.) in link interceptor

### Added

- Export `NavigationGuardOptions` and `NavigationGuardParams` types

## [1.0.1] - 2026-03-18

### Changed

- Updated README with full API documentation, migration guide, and fork explanation
- Updated CHANGELOG with fork history
- Updated LICENSE to include fork copyright

## [1.0.0] - 2026-03-18

Forked from [next-navigation-guard](https://github.com/LayerXcom/next-navigation-guard) v0.3.0
and published as `nextjs-nav-guard`.

### Added

- Centralized Next.js internal imports (`next/dist/*`) behind try/catch fallbacks for resilience
  across Next.js versions
- Local `AppRouterLike` type interface to avoid depending on Next.js internal type exports
- Dev-only console warning when `AppRouterContext` is unavailable (graceful degradation)
- Actionable error message with code example when `useNavigationGuard` is used without provider

### Fixed

- **Next.js 16.2 runtime crash:** added null guards on all `window.history.state` accesses
  in history augmentation, fixing `TypeError: Cannot read properties of null`
- **React rules-of-hooks violation:** fixed conditional `useContext` call in link click interceptor
- Removed dead code: unused `MutationObserver`, vestigial `needsInterceptor` ref,
  orphaned `_guardIntercepted` mutation
- Warn-once pattern for missing context warning (no console spam)

### Removed

- **Pages Router support:** removed `InterceptPagesRouterProvider`, `useInterceptedPagesRouter`,
  and all Pages Router code paths. App Router only.
- Self-referential dependency in package.json

### Changed

- Package renamed from `next-navigation-guard` to `nextjs-nav-guard`
- Debug log prefix changed to `[next-nav-guard]`
- DevDependencies updated to Next.js 16.2 and React 19

---

## Prior history (as `next-navigation-guard`)

### [0.3.0] - 2026-02-26

- Add `disableForTesting` option to `useNavigationGuard`
- Support Next.js 16 as peer dependency

### [0.2.0] - 2025-06-28

- Support for Next.js 15.3+ Link component
- Comprehensive E2E test suite using Playwright
- Support for React 19

### [0.1.2] - 2024-12-11

- Support Next.js 14 / 15 as peer dependencies

### [0.1.1] - 2024-10-07

- Fix back/forward button navigation

### [0.1.0] - 2024-09-18

- Initial release
